{{ 'ka-diary-featured.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- comment -%}
  K&A Client Diaries — Index Featured Diary. Docs/client-diaries-
  build-spec.md §2 row 3, §5 (data-modeling decision).

  DATA MODEL (chosen by Technical Director — spec §5 Option C,
  hybrid): each Client Diary entry is a Shopify BLOG ARTICLE in a
  dedicated blog (default handle "client-diaries", overridable
  below) — mirroring The Journal's proven index+entry+tag-filter
  pattern exactly (spec §5's own recommendation) — with a
  METAOBJECT type ("client_diary_look") holding the repeatable
  Looks list (spec field 6), referenced from the article via a
  list.metaobject_reference metafield. Metafields/metaobject used:

    Article metafields (namespace "custom"):
      client_diary_atelier_note   multi_line_text_field
      client_diary_consent        boolean   -- publishing gate, F3
      client_diary_year           single_line_text_field (optional
                                   override; falls back to the
                                   article's published year if unset)
      client_diary_looks          list.metaobject_reference ->
                                   client_diary_look

    NOT a new metafield — reused native Shopify fields instead:
      Client name         -> article.title (full name)
      Occasion             -> article.tags (fixed 4-value taxonomy,
                               identical mechanism to the Journal's
                               category tags)
      Client review        -> article.summary (native Excerpt field)
      Hero/cover image     -> article.image (native featured image),
                               falling back to the first Look's first
                               image if unset (spec field 8)
      Featured-entry pick  -> tag "featured", else most recent --
                               identical logic to ka-journal-featured.

    Metaobject "client_diary_look" fields:
      look_name        single_line_text_field
      look_description  multi_line_text_field
      look_images        list.file_reference (images only)
      cta_label          single_line_text_field (optional)
      category_link      url
      product_link        product_reference (optional; wins over
                           category_link when set -- spec field 6d)

  WHY THIS SHAPE (not blog+metafield-only, not metaobjects for the
  whole entry): the Journal's blog/tag/pagination machinery is
  already proven in production for "index of many + individual
  entry + occasion filter + empty state, growing indefinitely" --
  reusing it for the entry shell costs nothing and matches spec §5's
  explicit steer. The one place that machinery doesn't fit is the
  Looks repeater (spec F1: a variable-length ordered list of
  {image(s), title, description, link} groups) -- Shopify's native
  list.metaobject_reference metafield type is a first-class, staff-
  addable/reorderable ordered list for exactly this shape, which a
  single rich-text or JSON metafield would not offer as cleanly. This
  is spec §5 Option C (hybrid) named explicitly as an acceptable path.

  PUBLISHING GATE (F3): every Client Diaries section (this one,
  ka-diary-grid, and every ka-diary-entry-* section) independently
  checks client_diary_consent == true before rendering that article's
  name/images at all -- not merely a content field a staff member
  could forget to check. An article with consent unset/false is
  structurally invisible everywhere on the site, not just hidden by
  convention. See sections/ka-diary-entry-hero.liquid for the entry-
  page-side half of this gate.

  METAFIELD/METAOBJECT DEFINITION GAP (flagged per spec §5/F2, same
  category as the Journal's custom.breakout_image gap, 2026-08-08):
  as of this build (2026-08-10), NONE of the definitions above exist
  yet on this store (verified via Admin GraphQL
  metafieldDefinitions/metaobjectDefinitions — zero client_diary_*
  definitions found), and Technical Director's Admin API access is
  read-only (no graphql_mutation) -- cannot create them. Also: no
  "client-diaries" blog and no Simran article exist yet either (same
  read-only constraint -- creating Shopify content, not just theme
  code, requires write access this session doesn't have). See this
  build's final report for the full manual checklist required before
  Simran's entry (or any future entry) can go live.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign diary_blog = blogs[section.settings.blog_handle]
  assign featured_article = blank
  if diary_blog != blank
    for a in diary_blog.articles
      if a.metafields.custom.client_diary_consent == true and a.tags contains 'featured'
        assign featured_article = a
        break
      endif
    endfor
    if featured_article == blank
      for a in diary_blog.articles
        if a.metafields.custom.client_diary_consent == true
          assign featured_article = a
          break
        endif
      endfor
    endif
  endif
-%}

{%- if featured_article != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign occasion_label = 'Client Diary'
    assign occasion_handle = ''
    if featured_article.tags contains 'Bridal'
      assign occasion_label = 'Bridal'
      assign occasion_handle = 'bridal'
    elsif featured_article.tags contains 'Sangeet & Cocktail'
      assign occasion_label = 'Sangeet & Cocktail'
      assign occasion_handle = 'sangeet-cocktail'
    elsif featured_article.tags contains 'Festive'
      assign occasion_label = 'Festive'
      assign occasion_handle = 'festive'
    elsif featured_article.tags contains 'Mother & Family'
      assign occasion_label = 'Mother & Family'
      assign occasion_handle = 'mother-family'
    endif

    assign entry_year = featured_article.metafields.custom.client_diary_year
    if entry_year == blank
      assign entry_year = featured_article.published_at | date: '%Y'
    endif

    assign looks = featured_article.metafields.custom.client_diary_looks
    assign look_count = looks.size

    assign first_name = featured_article.title | split: ' ' | first

    assign hero_image = featured_article.image
    if hero_image == blank and look_count > 0
      assign hero_image = looks.first.look_images.first.image
    endif

    assign review_text = featured_article.summary | strip_html
    assign excerpt = featured_article.metafields.custom.client_diary_atelier_note | strip_html | truncate: 150
  -%}
  <section class="cd-featured" aria-label="Featured diary">
    <a href="{{ featured_article.url }}" class="cd-featured__image reveal-img">
      <span class="cd-featured__tag">{{ occasion_label }}</span>
      {%- if hero_image != blank -%}
        <img
          src="{{ hero_image | image_url: width: 1200 }}"
          alt="{{ hero_image.alt | escape | default: featured_article.title | escape }}"
          loading="lazy"
          width="1200"
          height="1400"
          class="img-filter-editorial"
        />
      {%- else -%}
        <img src="{{ 'cd-simran-maroon-1.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="{{ featured_article.title | escape }}" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="1400" class="img-filter-editorial" />
      {%- endif -%}
    </a>
    <div class="cd-featured__text">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--muted cd-featured__eyebrow reveal">Latest Diary</p>
      <h2 class="cd-featured__name reveal reveal-delay-1">{{ first_name }}&rsquo;s Diary</h2>
      <p class="cd-featured__meta reveal reveal-delay-1">
        {{ occasion_label }} <span>&middot;</span> {{ entry_year }}{% if look_count > 0 %} <span>&middot;</span> {{ look_count }} Look{% if look_count != 1 %}s{% endif %}{% endif %}
      </p>
      {%- if excerpt != blank -%}<p class="cd-featured__excerpt reveal reveal-delay-2">{{ excerpt }}</p>{%- endif -%}
      {%- if review_text != blank -%}<p class="cd-featured__quote reveal reveal-delay-2">{{ review_text | truncate: 180 }}</p>{%- endif -%}
      <div class="cd-featured__cta reveal reveal-delay-3"><a href="{{ featured_article.url }}" class="btn-dark">Read {{ first_name }}&rsquo;s Diary</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Diaries Featured",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "blog_handle",
      "label": "Client Diaries blog handle",
      "default": "client-diaries",
      "info": "Advanced. Must exactly match the handle of the Shopify blog used for Client Diaries entries."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Featured entry is chosen automatically from consented (published) entries only: whichever is tagged \"featured\", falling back to the most recent. No setting here selects it directly. The one-line excerpt reads from the entry's own \"From the Atelier\" note (custom.client_diary_atelier_note metafield), truncated; the pulled quote reads from the entry's native Excerpt field (article.summary)."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    { "name": "Diaries Featured" }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
